// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_budget_axis1.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: budget AXIS 1 (main-loop cycles) — the `ensure` inside
// engine/level/scene_dsl.emp's `scene_budget_enforce()`, which the shipped registry
// evaluates at games/sonic4/data/effects/scene_registry.emp's `SceneRegistry_BudgetChecked`.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "scene budget AXIS 1 (main-loop cycles)"
//
// THE TWO-FIXTURE DIFFERENTIAL (spec §8.2), and the unit is ONE BAND.
// RE-DERIVED BY P3 TASK 13 (2026-08-22): the model's promotion (post-unroll + re-glue rows,
// fitted anchor pair, uncertainty 11 -> 22 permil) and the re-derived reservation (23894 ->
// 24257) moved the crossing from 115/116 to 93/94. Integer mirror of the comptime math
// (x100, floor division exactly as scene_axis1_cycles_x100 computes it):
//   c(n)   = 311600 + 154800 + 85400(n-1) + 2000 + 98140 + 6077(3n-1)
//   tot(n) = c + c*22/1000;   guard: tot/100 + 24257 <= 128000
//
//   FIXTURE A — 93 bands. Costs 103352.26 cyc against a 103743-cyc budget: 391 cyc of
//               headroom. PASSES, and it must: an ensure that only ever fires is
//               indistinguishable from one that is stuck, so the passing half is half the
//               assertion.
//   FIXTURE B — THE SAME SCENE with 94 bands. Costs 104411.37. FAILS by 668 cycles, which
//               is the smallest overrun the model's own granularity admits, because one
//               band IS the smallest thing an author can add and one band's marginal is
//               1059.1 cyc (854.00 band_perline + 3 x 60.77 anchor trips, x1.022).
//
// A and B differ in exactly one field, `sc_count`. Under the promoted model that moves TWO
// fitted slopes rather than one — `band_perline_cycles` 854.00 applied once more, and the
// anchored overlay's worst-case trip count 3n-1 growing by three `anchor_ops_cycles` 60.77
// — because the anchor is a fitted (base + per-trip) pair since P3 Task 1, not a flat
// worst-regime constant. Nothing else moves — same (absent) table, same anchor CHANNEL,
// same absent V-deform, so the base, line-mode, multiband and sampling terms are identical
// across the pair and the whole difference is the per-band slope pair the fixture probes.
//
// ---- WHY THIS POISON USES THE `Scene{ .. }` BACK DOOR, AND WHY THAT IS THE HONEST SHAPE ----
//
// `scene()` caps `count` at MAX_PARALLAX_BANDS, so NO scene built through the
// constructor can reach 94 — and at 8 bands the worst possible constructor scene (both
// planes sampling at shift 14, a curve layer, V-deform, anchored, every worst-case charge
// stacked) costs 67549.93 cyc against the 103743 budget, i.e. 65%. THAT IS A REAL PROPERTY
// OF THE SHIPPED MODEL AND IT IS RECORDED RATHER THAN HIDDEN: the constructor surface
// cannot cross the axis-1 budget (though the promoted model's new worst-case terms — shift,
// per-sampling-band, per-trip anchor — closed most of the P2-era ~9x gap), so its practical
// role is a ledger row plus a BACKSTOP, and the thing it backstops is precisely the
// hand-built `Scene{ .. }` literal.
//
// That back door is documented twice in engine/level/scene_dsl.emp (at the `Scene` and
// `SceneLayer` struct banners) and it is real: a literal type-checks and bypasses the pad
// guard, the mask-superset guard, both ported anchor guards and the precision fence in one
// go. `assert_act_relative_tagged()` exists at REGISTRY level for exactly this reason — it
// is the only place a value that came through that door can still be caught. This poison
// probes the budget fold the same way, at the same level, for the same reason.
//
// A poison that instead moved a CONSTANT (shrank the pool, grew the reservation) would prove
// only that arithmetic is arithmetic. This one perturbs the SUBJECT — the scene's own cost —
// which is what "every poison must perturb the SUBJECT and name the specific mismatch"
// requires.
//
// ---- WHY THE LAYER ARRAY IS MAX_PARALLAX_BANDS ELEMENTS WHILE sc_count SAYS 93/94 ----
//
// `sc_layers` is a fixed `[SceneLayer; 16]`; the count is a separate field, which is exactly
// how the back door produces an inconsistent value in the first place. Nothing in the axis-1
// path INDEXES the array for this fixture: with no deform table attached,
// `scene_sample_term_x100()` short-circuits at `scene_has_table()` and never reaches
// `scene_live_amp_a/b()`, which are the only functions that walk layers. So the fixture
// exercises the band-slope arithmetic and nothing else, deliberately.
//
// THE ELABORATION HOOK is the two ensures below reading the two consts, which forces
// `scene_budget_enforce()` — and through it every axis function — to elaborate. Expected
// `[Error]` count is 1: fixture B trips AXIS 1 only. Its axis-2 and axis-3 charges are
// unchanged from fixture A's and both fit with room to spare (a per-line scene costs 896 B
// against a 5364 B budget and 2135 cyc against 9920), so neither of those ensures fires.
// A count of 2 means another axis started failing; a count of 0 means the fold stopped
// distinguishing 93 bands from 94.
//
// THE GLOB IMPORTS ARE THE AUTHOR'S OWN SPELLING — see README.md ("Why every scene poison globs").
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_budget_axis1

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

// The eight-element pad. Every entry is a dormant no_layer(); none is read on this path.
const POISON_A1_PADS: [SceneLayer; 16] = [
    no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
    no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
                                          no_layer(),
                                          no_layer(),
                                          no_layer(),
                                          no_layer(),
                                          no_layer(),
                                          no_layer(),
                                          no_layer(),
                                          no_layer()]

// FIXTURE A — 93 bands, the last count that fits.
const POISON_A1_SCENE_A: Scene = Scene{
    sc_layers:             POISON_A1_PADS,
    sc_count:              93,
    sc_v_factor:           3,
    sc_v_center:           0,
    sc_v_offset:           0,
    sc_v_factor_fg:        0,
    sc_deform_fg:          SceneDeform.None,
    sc_deform_bg:          SceneDeform.None,
    sc_v_deform:           SceneVDeform.None,
    // Anchored, both shifts at 15: this is what puts the scene on the per-line pipeline
    // WITHOUT attaching a table, so the sampling term stays 0 and the layer array is
    // never walked. The anchor's fitted BASE (981.4) is charged identically to both
    // fixtures and cancels out of the differential; its per-trip slope does NOT (worst
    // trips = 3n-1 grows with the count) and is half of what the pair probes.
    sc_anchor:             SceneAnchor.At(0, 15, 15),
    // P3 Task 12: the back door spells the policy field like every other attachment's
    // None — Undeclared is legal here because neither fixture attaches a v-deform table.
    sc_left_col_mask:      SceneLeftColMask.Undeclared,
    sc_transition:         0,
    // NO BOB — spelled, not defaulted, because engine/level/scene_dsl.emp gives
    // sc_bob_shift / sc_bob_period no field default on purpose: this back door bypasses
    // scene() and every guard in it, so a Scene literal has to STATE the vertical bob the
    // way it already states its left-column policy. 15 is the no-bob sentinel. Both
    // fields are inert to this poison, which measures the walker's main-loop cycle cost —
    // the bob's 26 cycles a frame live in Step 5, not in the walker.
    sc_bob_shift:          15,
    sc_bob_period:         0,
    sc_pad_5D:             default,
    sc_mask_raw:           -1,
    sc_v_deform_shift_raw: -1,
}

// FIXTURE B — byte-for-byte fixture A except for `sc_count`: one more band.
const POISON_A1_SCENE_B: Scene = Scene{
    sc_layers:             POISON_A1_PADS,
    sc_count:              94,
    sc_v_factor:           3,
    sc_v_center:           0,
    sc_v_offset:           0,
    sc_v_factor_fg:        0,
    sc_deform_fg:          SceneDeform.None,
    sc_deform_bg:          SceneDeform.None,
    sc_v_deform:           SceneVDeform.None,
    sc_anchor:             SceneAnchor.At(0, 15, 15),
    // P3 Task 12: the back door spells the policy field like every other attachment's
    // None — Undeclared is legal here because neither fixture attaches a v-deform table.
    sc_left_col_mask:      SceneLeftColMask.Undeclared,
    sc_transition:         0,
    // NO BOB — spelled, not defaulted, because engine/level/scene_dsl.emp gives
    // sc_bob_shift / sc_bob_period no field default on purpose: this back door bypasses
    // scene() and every guard in it, so a Scene literal has to STATE the vertical bob the
    // way it already states its left-column policy. 15 is the no-bob sentinel. Both
    // fields are inert to this poison, which measures the walker's main-loop cycle cost —
    // the bob's 26 cycles a frame live in Step 5, not in the walker.
    sc_bob_shift:          15,
    sc_bob_period:         0,
    sc_pad_5D:             default,
    sc_mask_raw:           -1,
    sc_v_deform_shift_raw: -1,
}

// ---- FIXTURE A, THE PASSING HALF (this must stay green) ----
// `scene_budget_enforce` returns the number of scenes it checked, so referencing it is what
// evaluates the fold — an unreferenced top-level const is comptime-INERT and would prove
// nothing (docs/EMP_PITFALLS.md §3).
const POISON_A1_CHECKED_A = scene_budget_enforce([POISON_A1_SCENE_A])
ensure(POISON_A1_CHECKED_A == 1,
       "poison_budget_axis1: FIXTURE A did not pass the budget fold cleanly (checked {POISON_A1_CHECKED_A}) — the passing half of the differential no longer holds, so fixture B failing below proves nothing about the band slope")

// ---- FIXTURE B, THE POISON (this is the diagnostic the lane matches) ----
const POISON_A1_CHECKED_B = scene_budget_enforce([POISON_A1_SCENE_B])
ensure(POISON_A1_CHECKED_B == 1,
       "poison_budget_axis1: FIXTURE B was expected to trip AXIS 1 — one more band than fixture A's 93, i.e. one more band_perline_cycles (854.00) plus three more anchor trips (3 x 60.77) on top of a cost already 391 cyc from the ceiling")
